        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "5e219e42-0a96-3aea-af7c-ebeff5833510",
                "word": "atavique",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "773d9639-810b-4367-9e2a-89f405a2cac6",
                        "entry_id": "5e219e42-0a96-3aea-af7c-ebeff5833510",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "ataviques"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "37615727-76c6-362c-b5f4-bdfaceeac498",
                        "entry_id": "5e219e42-0a96-3aea-af7c-ebeff5833510",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui se transmet par atavisme ; relatif à l’atavisme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "48fa7dca-e947-46df-952f-5473131cdd27",
                                "sense_id": "37615727-76c6-362c-b5f4-bdfaceeac498",
                                "text": "Des fautes comme les miennes, que je ne tente pas d’expliquer par l’influence des fatalités ataviques, et par les pernicieux effets d’une éducation si contraire à ma nature, ont besoin d’une expiation terrible, et cette expiation que j’ai choisie, elle est dans la confession publique de ma vie."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a337d875-4a86-490d-b2a3-4daf42d4dc59",
                                "sense_id": "37615727-76c6-362c-b5f4-bdfaceeac498",
                                "text": "Nous autres du corps enseignant, sommes plus sensibles que quiconque à la conservation des qualités ataviques, qui ont fait la grandeur de la France."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "73746fcf-5dc6-4716-9ed9-0e38731c2364",
                                "sense_id": "37615727-76c6-362c-b5f4-bdfaceeac498",
                                "text": "Il éprouvait le besoin de se coucher sur la neige. Mais l’atavique et sûr instinct de sa conservation l’avertissait de ne pas s’abandonner à ce désir. — (James Oliver Curwood, Kazan, 1914, traduit de l’anglais par P. Gruyer et L. Postif, Hachette, 1937, page 45)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3833e25e-9e1a-463c-a55a-46c659b8f0c0",
                                "sense_id": "37615727-76c6-362c-b5f4-bdfaceeac498",
                                "text": "Ce remarquable comportement des anguilles et leur nostophilie (mémoire atavique d’un habitat ancestral) ont donné lieu à certaines théories des plus intéressantes ; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e6dd609-b371-4027-b793-dae76f2169cc",
                                "sense_id": "37615727-76c6-362c-b5f4-bdfaceeac498",
                                "text": "Depuis, tous partis confondus – CAQ, PLQ, PQ et QS –, les chefs se bousculent pour dénoncer cette énième manifestation du mépris classique des élites anglo-canadiennes envers la présumée « intolérance » atavique des francophones pour les minorités."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7914ed90-4de7-3588-89fe-696cd1464925",
                        "entry_id": "5e219e42-0a96-3aea-af7c-ebeff5833510",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ancestral."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "96075745-79b8-4f71-bcd0-40de866377a7",
                                "sense_id": "7914ed90-4de7-3588-89fe-696cd1464925",
                                "text": "Ils n’avaient d’autre ambition que celle de trouver leur place dans le village, se pliant au rythme atavique des normes établies et ne dérangeant rien de ce microcosme."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "61cb906a-90c7-4591-8846-a1b149805f46",
                        "source_entry_id": "5e219e42-0a96-3aea-af7c-ebeff5833510",
                        "source_sense_description": "relatif à l’atavisme",
                        "target_lang_word": "atavistisch",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "atavistisch",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b7316208-828f-3647-9e83-c935960e5daf",
                                        "entry_id": "d7cd14f3-244c-34b0-8fc4-fdddedf50fcf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "uralt und überholt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6453a3d0-f27e-4cfa-af39-4cec37b3d87e",
                                                "sense_id": "b7316208-828f-3647-9e83-c935960e5daf",
                                                "text": "„Die Fremdenfeindlichkeit ging so bald einher mit der atavistischen Neigung, den Boten für die überbrachte Nachricht verantwortlich zu machen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d45ea97c-cfb0-4105-a754-6c51945c00c9",
                        "source_entry_id": "5e219e42-0a96-3aea-af7c-ebeff5833510",
                        "source_sense_description": "relatif à l’atavisme",
                        "target_lang_word": "atavistic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "atavistic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "11720ab7-c6ce-3a7d-9408-8e2070775710",
                                        "entry_id": "2cbec3b7-c875-3cf0-b70e-d77b801c4737",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of the recurrence of a trait reappearing after an absence of one or more generations due to a chance recombination of genes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9e88491-5816-400a-85f4-ed2b8ec7efab",
                                                "sense_id": "11720ab7-c6ce-3a7d-9408-8e2070775710",
                                                "text": "Although the heterozygote gives it an atavistic appearance, the gene is not atavistic."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12cc4373-14d0-4afa-98cc-687cb9fd8090",
                                                "sense_id": "11720ab7-c6ce-3a7d-9408-8e2070775710",
                                                "text": "Thus the gene which produced atavistic digits in the vigorous heterozygous pentadactyl condition is a lethal monster in the homozygous condition."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd4cd543-05e7-4589-abbb-d534c4a1775e",
                                                "sense_id": "11720ab7-c6ce-3a7d-9408-8e2070775710",
                                                "text": "Reactivation of a dormant atavistic gene could account for the abnormal costocoracoid ligament in humans."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "51dabfcc-222d-3c38-8e34-455418724a95",
                                        "entry_id": "2cbec3b7-c875-3cf0-b70e-d77b801c4737",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a throwback or exhibiting primitivism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12145801-4d91-42c5-9d4f-0e79451755ff",
                                                "sense_id": "51dabfcc-222d-3c38-8e34-455418724a95",
                                                "text": "They made me feel that I was alive in the nineteenth century, a sort of atavistic remnant, a romantic shred […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a88e38b-ec45-4719-aa87-f0eda1c7a0b4",
                                                "sense_id": "51dabfcc-222d-3c38-8e34-455418724a95",
                                                "text": "The true perversion took place only in the privacy of her mind — the way she imagined an atavistic macho atop her when engaged in a mandatory contribution to the fetus-banks with some cretinous inept breeder…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8331c06-f914-4d6b-b5c3-2b10a93299cd",
                                                "sense_id": "51dabfcc-222d-3c38-8e34-455418724a95",
                                                "text": "Because I am atavistic enough to believe that drawing is the basic language of the illustrator, even as words comprise the basic language of the writer…"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7f4a495a-1e6d-398c-965c-8436b6db25e3",
                                        "entry_id": "2cbec3b7-c875-3cf0-b70e-d77b801c4737",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relating to earlier, more primitive behavior that returns after an absence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
